        significance: 'Paul has spent three chapters establishing universal guilt before God (Romans 1-3:20) before this explosive "But now." The justified sinner stands in right relationship with God not because of personal merit but because of Christ\'s propitiatory sacrifice — His blood satisfying divine justice. The word "justified" (*dikaioō*) is a legal term meaning declared righteous. God does not pretend sin didn\'t happen; He punishes it in His Son so that the sinner can be genuinely acquitted.',
