        text: 'Now the law came in to increase the trespass, but where sin increased, grace abounded all the more, so that, as sin reigned in death, grace also might reign through righteousness leading to eternal life through Jesus Christ our Lord.',
        significance: 'Paul\'s argument here reaches its crescendo: grace does not merely match sin — it overwhelms it. The verb "abounded all the more" (Greek: *huperperisseuō*) means to super-abound, to overflow beyond all measure. No catalogue of human sin can exceed the reach of divine grace. But Paul immediately anticipates the misuse of this truth: "Are we to continue in sin that grace may abound? By no means!" (Romans 6:1-2). Grace that truly reigns does so through righteousness — it produces holiness, not license.',
        category: 'Pauline Epistles',
