        significance: 'The Incarnation is the supreme historical event of grace. The eternal Word becoming flesh is itself the ultimate undeserved gift — God giving His Son to dwell among the very creatures who would reject Him (John 1:11). The phrase "grace upon grace" (*charin anti charitos*) suggests grace flowing in waves, each one replaced by another — an inexhaustible supply from Christ\'s infinite fullness. John deliberately contrasts law (given through Moses) with grace and truth (came through Christ), marking a covenantal transition.',
