        definition: 'Derived from the root *aman* meaning to be firm, established, reliable, or confirmed. Emunah is not merely intellectual belief but settled trustworthiness — a reliability that holds firm under pressure. When used of humans it describes the faithfulness and integrity of a person who keeps their word. When used of God it describes His absolute covenantal reliability.',
