        transliteration: 'amen',
        definition: 'A word of confirmation and affirmation derived from the same root as emunah. When used at the end of a prayer or declaration it means "this is certain, this is reliable, I commit to this." Jesus uniquely used it at the beginning of statements (*Amen, amen, I say to you*) to claim divine authority for His words rather than merely responding to them.',
