        significance: '"The wrath of the Lamb" (*orgē tou arniou*) is one of the most jarring oxymorons in Scripture — the Lamb, symbol of gentle sacrifice (John 1:29, Isaiah 53:7), becomes the source of cosmic wrath. The same Jesus who died to absorb God\'s wrath will execute God\'s wrath on those who refused His sacrifice. The universal flight of every level of human society — from kings to slaves — before the divine face indicates that wrath at the final judgment will be unavoidable. The rhetorical question "Who can stand?" (echoing Psalm 76:7 and Malachi 3:2) has only one answer: those whose sin has already been absorbed by the Lamb.',
