        significance: '"Wait for the LORD" (*qawah el YHWH*) — the Hebrew root *qawah* means to twist or bind together, like strands into a rope. Waiting on the LORD is not passive resignation but active expectation — the binding of one\'s hope tightly to God\'s character and promises. The sequence of restoration (wings → running → walking) is deliberately descending in intensity: the most dramatic burst of renewal is followed by sustained endurance (running), which is ultimately expressed in the ordinary (walking). Spiritual growth often looks less spectacular and more faithful as it matures.',
        category: 'Prophets',
