        significance: 'Jesus\' teaching on church discipline (the only passage in the Gospels besides Matthew 16 where *ekklēsia* appears) establishes the church as the community with authority to maintain its covenantal boundaries and to seek restoration of straying members. The process is relational (one-on-one), then communal, and finally ecclesial — always aiming at restoration, never at punishment. The promise of Christ\'s presence among "two or three gathered in my name" grounds even the smallest local gathering in the real, authoritative presence of the risen Lord — making no assembly too small or too imperfect to be a genuine church.',
