        significance: 'Paul attributes to Christ the divine prerogatives of creation, sovereignty, and cosmic sustenance. "Image of the invisible God" (eikōn tou theou tou aoratou) means Christ is the visible manifestation of God\'s nature. "Firstborn" (prōtotokos) denotes supremacy of rank, not origin. "Before all things" affirms eternality. "In him all things hold together" ascribes the moment-by-moment sustaining of the universe to the Son.',
